Cell["\<\
This makes the Crown resemblance precise. The three-loop Crown is K4,2. The \
present graph is a maximal Crown-defective bipartite completion: neither pair \
among e,f,g connects to all four attachment vertices, but adding either \
missing edge immediately creates a literal K4,2 Crown subgraph. Adding one \
edge gives E=11, V=7, hence five loops; completing K4,3 gives E=12, V=7, \
hence six loops and contains all three possible K4,2 subgraphs. Therefore \
complete K4,3 is not a new five-loop seed. The natural five-loop completion \
already contains the known Crown seed, although it could still support \
additional regions beyond the inherited one.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"29a28841-ea60-4667-8f0f-54e71561b868"],

