Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["7. Why long derivative factors cannot reopen the result", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"26a604c2-4979-4459-9c19-9c9b8c79f846"],

Cell["\<\
The historical eight-monomial cutoff has been removed from HRF: \
$HRFPolynomialMaxDerivativeMonomials is now fixed to Infinity, and the \
current raw harvest resets its per-polynomial state on every stratum. The \
uncapped factor prefilter consequently retains many more candidate \
presentations. None of those presentations can evade the face/pinch proof, \
because any HR\[LongDash]whatever generators or polynomial multipliers \
describe it\[LongDash]must select one of the enumerated F0 faces and satisfy \
the same pinch and hierarchy equations.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"f8cd5877-2e24-4c2b-b9a6-36ea1ea37483"],

Cell["\<\
The graph-theoretic observation 'no Crown contraction minor' therefore \
remains a useful classifier, but it is not used as the proof. The proof is \
the stronger polynomial statement: every possible F_SL face is \
subtraction-free, has a sign-definite derivative, or has a subtraction-free \
linear combination of logarithmic derivatives; any exceptional positive pinch \
would still have to pass the exact hierarchy LP.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"15d936dc-8349-4a5e-a05e-bc978b273c10"],

Cell["\<\
This sharpens the earlier evidence at the bottom of p. 19 of \
arXiv:2407.13738, where the individual channel coefficients admitted separate \
solutions but no common solution was found when both wide-angle invariants \
were active.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"8c3a6185-2155-47c7-b448-94f8f89eee07"]
}, Open  ]],

